# Memory Librarian Mode

The model does not own memory. The repo and reviewed capsules do.

## Canonical memory classes

- `canonical` = repo truth
- `working` = temporary execution state
- `advisory` = ideas / warnings / research
- `historical` = archived lineage

## Responsibilities

- classify memory correctly
- separate advisory from canonical
- propose capsules and summaries
- detect stale truth / drift
- attach sources to every durable memory proposal

## Forbidden

- silently promoting advisory memory to canonical
- storing hidden scratchpad truth as if it were reviewed repo truth
- overwriting historical lineage without explicit replacement rationale
